    "prompt": "Below is a description of the Python function `_tempfilepager`.\n\nDescription:\n\"\"\"\nThe `_tempfilepager` function is designed to display the contents of a generator of strings using an external command, typically a pager like `less` or `more`. It creates a temporary file, writes the generator's content to this file, and then invokes the specified command to open and display the file. The function accepts three parameters: `generator`, which is an iterable of strings to be displayed; `cmd`, the command to use for displaying the file; and `color`, a boolean indicating whether to strip ANSI color codes from the text before writing it to the file. The function does not return any value; its purpose is to perform the side effect of displaying the text. It relies on the `tempfile.mkstemp` function to create a temporary file, `strip_ansi` to remove color codes if necessary, and `get_best_encoding` to determine the appropriate encoding for writing to the file. The function handles errors by ensuring that the temporary file is properly closed and deleted in a `finally` block, regardless of whether the command execution succeeds or fails.\n\"\"\"\n\nSplit the description into atomic claims. Each claim must be a single, self-contained factual statement about the function that could be checked against the function's source code (name the function explicitly; no pronouns referring to other claims). Do not add claims that are not in the description; do not merge two facts into one claim. Keep the original wording where possible. Assign each claim exactly one type:\n- \"structural\": the function's signature, parameter names/defaults/types, return type, or which functions, methods, classes or attributes it uses.\n- \"dataflow\": how a value is computed, transformed, passed on, or what is returned for which input.\n- \"behavioural\": exceptions raised or caught, conditions/early returns, side effects, edge-case handling, ordering/iteration behaviour.\n- \"intent\": purpose, rationale, or the role of the function in the larger system.\n\nReturn a JSON array of at most 12 objects: [{\"text\": \"...\", \"type\": \"structural|dataflow|behavioural|intent\"}, ...]",
